From f93b0b5cb09f5f0bd1807f2a735ee5f6456d2210 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patch Author <patch@local>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 10:31:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(identity): real per-subscriber accounts, remove fake
 mock plan fallback
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Every visitor previously shared one hardcoded 'default-user' ID on the
backend, and onboarding only ever wrote to that browser's local
IndexedDB — nothing was genuinely per-person. Separately, if the diet-plan
API call failed for any reason, the app silently displayed a fully
fabricated 7-day plan with invented foods and numbers, indistinguishable
from a real one.

New:
- lib/identity/subscriberId.ts — creates a real backend subscriber
  account on first visit (POST /api/subscribers), caches the ID
  locally. No phone/OTP here — that's the separate Bdapps subscription
  feature, built later. This just makes accounts real.

Changed:
- useNutritionStore: subscriberId now starts empty and is populated by
  a real initSubscriber() action, not a hardcoded constant. setProfile
  writes through to POST /api/profile (local cache remains for
  responsiveness/offline, but is no longer the only place data lives).
  loadProfile tries the real server first, distinguishing 'no profile
  yet' (404, expected for new accounts) from an actual network failure
  (falls back to local cache only in that case).
- The entire ~150-line hardcoded mock diet plan is deleted. On a real
  failure, the store now sets a plain planError message instead of
  fabricating data — showing invented food as if it were a real plan
  is worse than a clear, retryable error.
- Every hardcoded http://localhost:3001 across the web app (store,
  admin page, progress page) replaced with the existing
  NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL-based helper — was a deployment blocker before.
- app/(app)/layout.tsx now blocks rendering any page until a real
  subscriber account exists (with a loading state and a real retry UI
  on failure), so no page can ever run against an empty/fake ID.
- OnboardingFlow submits under the real subscriberId instead of a
  hardcoded 'default-user' fallback.

Verified: full workspace build + real 'next build' production build +
all 80 existing tests pass + live end-to-end walkthrough against a real
Postgres database — created two different subscribers through the real
API, gave them different profiles (build_muscle/bengali vs.
lose_weight/western), confirmed both their profiles and generated diet
plans landed as fully independent rows, verified directly in Postgres
independent of the running server.

Known follow-up (not in scope here): loadLogsForDate still only reads
from local IndexedDB — food logs sync up to the server but don't yet
sync down on a new device. Worth a dedicated pass, not blocking this.
